{"title":"datasette-agent 0.5a0","link":"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/3/datasette-agent/","date":1793747625000,"content":"\n    \n        <p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-agent/releases/tag/0.5a0\">datasette-agent 0.5a0</a></p>\n        <p>This is a significant release of <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\">Datasette Agent</a>. The most notable new feature is called the <strong>panel</strong> - it lets the agent chat open and then sit next to pages from Datasette, for example a table or query page.</p>\n<p>When combined with <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-apps\">datasette-apps</a> this means you can prompt a database-backed app into existence and then modify it from the chat that sits next to that app.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot of a split-screen chat interface titled &quot;evaluate llm prices&quot; (model tag &quot;gpt-6-luna&quot;): the conversation runs in a narrow column on the left, and a wide side panel on the right displays the app the assistant built, with &quot;EXPORT&quot; and &quot;Close panel&quot; buttons above it. In the chat, blue user bubbles read &quot;Build an app to help explore this data&quot; and &quot;give it a more hacker aesthetic design&quot;, each followed by collapsed tool calls (app_create, app_render, app_view, app_str_replace), &quot;LLM Price Explorer v1.&quot; and &quot;v2.&quot; entries with &quot;View app&quot; and &quot;Edit&quot; buttons, and short assistant replies describing the app and its new dark terminal-inspired theme. The right panel shows the resulting &quot;LLM Price Explorer&quot; in neon green monospace on black: stat cards for 185 models from 12 providers with workload costs from $0.042 (Jev 1.13) to $300.00 (o1 Pro), filter and workload cost estimate controls, and a table of matching models with input, output and cached input prices per million tokens.\" src=\"/media/0a86ad00698418c564249b5d5c8caafde3e0f4cddfd11c157b75a01183d52395.webp\" /></p>\n<p>You can try it by signing in with your GitHub account to <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\">agent.datasette.io</a>.</p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/projects\">projects</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-agent\">datasette-agent</a></p>\n    \n\n","author":"Simon Willison","siteTitle":"Simon Willison’s Weblog","siteHash":"1b599216bd27a00f15d67a3ed9719c64148630c70244b6dd8e743f17cb45527e","entryHash":"f81a8762c1d701e0ef3fbd8cd2f5494db3edccc1de4bd29db7bb822f1b9ec13c","category":"Tech"}